{
  "_about": "D&D locations and minis (docs/DND-3D-GOAL.md). A location's map is an ASCII layout, one string per row. Walkable: '.' floor, ',' road, '=' bridge deck, '~' difficult terrain (costs double), 'D' door, 'P' a player spawn, 'M' a monster spawn. Blocking: '#' wall, 'T' tree, 'R' rock, 'O' pillar, 'K' table, 'B' barrel, 'S' sarcophagus, 'C' cart, 'W' deep water. The theme says how scripts/dnd_room_blender.py draws them. Files live in R2 under dnd/locations/<id>/ (room.glb, map.jpg, view.jpg; art.jpg and shot.mp4 from Cosmos 3) and locally in table/.cache/dnd/; a location without them still plays on the grid. status: 'draft' until a person approves it in /dnd/review.",
